WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.552
A grounded prompt can explicitly require use of the supplied context, citations after factual claims,

00:00:07.552 --> 00:00:10.867
and a clear abstention when the evidence is missing.

00:00:10.867 --> 00:00:12.942
Those instructions help, but they are not guarantees.

00:00:12.942 --> 00:00:21.837
The final application should still evaluate whether the answer is supported by the retrieved sources.

00:00:21.837 --> 00:00:26.272
The abstention rule is just as important as the citation rule.

00:00:26.272 --> 00:00:31.830
A grounded system should be allowed to say that the provided evidence does not contain the answer.
